Yes, absolutely. Your project is on React 18, so `useTransition` is available out of the box:

```jsx
import { useTransition } from 'react';

function SearchBox() {
  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition();
  // ...
}
```

Since you're already on 18 you also get automatic batching and `useDeferredValue` for free, so I'd lean on those for the search-as-you-type work rather than the old debounce utility. No dependency changes needed — just import and go.

